<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Marius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">157–86 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Marius was a Roman general and politician who held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">consulship</a> seven times. He ended the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a> of Numidia, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri">Cimbri</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutones">Teutones</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aix-en-provence">Aquae Sextiae</a> and Vercellae, and opened the legions to men without property. His rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a> led to the civil wars of 88 to 82 BCE, and his followers, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-sertorius">Quintus Sertorius</a>, fought on after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaius-marius.jpg" alt="Gaius Marius" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: American Numismatic Society · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RRC_326.1_Gaius_Fundanius_depicting_Gaius_Marius_triumphator.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
